WEBVTT

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:14.380
It is clear that our bloodline has been 
around since the long past Heian period.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.020
Just because we're tanuki

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.920
doesn't mean we're popped out of

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.660
a nook in a camphor tree
 like a hairy ball of candy.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.380
The wildly branching bloodline we inherit

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.590
somehow binds us.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.330
Even for a Bohemian tanuki like me

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:40.830
blood ties cannot be so easily abandoned.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:45.790
As you might expect, even just tenuous blood 
relation can keep slight quarrels from being forgotten,

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:50.180
so instead of water under the bridge 
they become feuds.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.780
"Blood is thicker than water"

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.960
is a saying that is more than I can handle.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.000
<b>Episode 7: Bathhouse Rules</b>

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.250
<b>Akegarasu</b>

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.650
Did you find what you were looking for?

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.350
I don't even have a clue.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:43.620
But still, I thought you had already 
been boiled in a hot pot and eaten!

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.880
Well, I'm sure it'll happen sometime, 
so there's not much of a difference.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.010
With all due respect, what the hell.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.000
You should drink while you can.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.570
Carpe diem.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.790
Big Brother, save me.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.620
He hates baths. To an extreme degree.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.190
Despite the times being such that even tanuki 
who make their home in the forest of Shimogamo

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:12.530
worry about split ends and treat their hair,

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.620
it's so bad he even hates wiping 
his body with a damp cloth.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.640
Oh so that's why. I'll say,
 "Let's go to the bathhouse!" and he'll be like,

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.280
"The weather's bad." "My butt 
itches." "My back hurts."

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.890
"I don't like the look on your face!"

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.330
You didn't try to drag him out?

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.920
I did! And he threw a heavy Daruma at me.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:38.210
Anyways, the room is enveloped in this 
complex aroma like something is fermenting,

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.860
so I tried to do something, but...

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:44.630
But he's spraying so much perfume 
you can't even breathe?

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.940
Yeah.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.830
Big Brother, I'm useless.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:52.310
I can't get the professor 
to take a bath or anything.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:56.840
Don't cry Yashiro. It's 
a useless talent to have.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.880
You have better things to master.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.560
He's blowing tengu winds.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.190
Oh, he has enough energy left to do that?

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:09.190
It puts kinks in my hair.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.170
Any more and I'll end up with an afro.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:16.360
To show off the remnants of his 
former power to a little kid,

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.720
he's a disgrace to all tengu.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.370
I'm gonna hurl him into the steaming water!

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:26.330
But Big Brother, you shouldn't 
bully him too much.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:29.340
I know. I just wanted to say that.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.040
Hey, your tail.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.160
Is that Yasaburo?

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:48.820
I haven't seen you since the 
night of the Fire Festival.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:51.260
Where have you been loafing about?

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.790
You're a lowlife who has forgotten 
how to act towards his mentor.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.830
All you think about is having fun.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:05:01.210
It's not as if I was screwing around, but... 
anyways, I apologize for not visiting sooner.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.550
I have no need for your visits.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:06.200
It was a load off of my mind 
not having you around.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:08.800
Oh, you're always saying that.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.080
Why not just admit you were lonely?

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.780
As if!

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:21.880
Why does someone like me have to go 
take a bath accompanied by you tanuki?

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.330
You don't want to go with us? Is that it?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.040
So you would go if it were with Benten?

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.100
That goes without saying. 
That's exactly what I want.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.490
You lech of a tengu.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:37.950
In that case, how about 
I transform into Benten?

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.400
With an erotic bounce...

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.990
Just try it. I'll crush you!

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:46.600
If you're gonna do it, then do it, 
you stubborn old tengu!

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.580
You asked for it.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:53.220
You guys are nothing against my tengu wind 
if I feel like whipping it.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.050
Bring it!

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.630
Yasaburo, what are you playing at over there?

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:39.700
Sheesh.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.940
No more of this "moo moo" nonsense.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:46.320
Professor, did getting into a temper 
perhaps cause you to sweat?

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.770
Mm.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:51.060
Having a bath now and then 
is not such a bad thing.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.870
Mm.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:02.960
Professor, it's been some time.

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.580
It's cold out, huh, Yaichiro.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.280
Yes, Professor.

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:11.140
This is some pain in the neck, huh.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.670
Not at all.

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.250
Say what you really think!

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.330
I'm speaking from the heart.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.130
Well, whatever.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.920
Okay, let's go! 
What are we farting around for?

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.590
<b>Bathhouse</b>

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:35.530
What a bother, oh bother.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:37.790
<b>Women</b>

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.180
Big Brother, this bath is cold!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:23.420
Yashiro, that was a cold soak to begin with.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:28.920
Why do I have to take a 
bath with you hairballs?

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:33.390
Since we're in human form, there is no 
need for concern regarding shedding.

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:37.500
Either way, I wish Benten 
were here to wash my back.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:40.450
I want to take a bath with Benten.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:43.610
Ahhh, I wanna take a bath with Benteeeeen!

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:46.990
Professor, such an open 
display of indecent desire!

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:49.840
Please try to preserve a bit of honor.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.630
I'm ashamed to be your disciple.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:56.940
Even if Benten came, you wouldn't be 
able to go in the women's bath anyways.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.090
Shush!

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:00.830
Yasaburo,

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:05.340
isn't it true that you were out the other 
day with Benten and the Friday Fellows?

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:09.830
It really does seem like you have an 
unreasonable penchant for following her around.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:15.140
It couldn't be that a hairball like you 
is carrying a torch for her...?

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:19.250
Don't be ridiculous. What's the point 
of a tanuki falling for a human?

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.120
Forbidden love?

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.820
As if you give a damn about tanuki laws.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:29.510
Who knows what a twisted 
guy like you is plotting.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:32.280
You pick some weird stuff to get hung up on.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:36.360
I'm just concerned for your well-being.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:40.930
If you make light of her as 
just some human girl, you'll be eaten up.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.630
Professor!

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:52.180
It's about time to get out.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:55.630
You're not gonna let me take my time washing

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:58.610
even though you're the one 
who told me to take a bath?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:03.490
Ugh, he says he hates baths, 
but once he gets in he never gets out.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.200
Tastes sweet.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.670
Sure does.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:13.090
Big Brother, coffee and milk both taste bad,

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.880
so why does coffee milk taste good?

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.980
That's the multiplier effect.

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:20.110
Multiplier effect?

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.710
A fateful encounter.

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:25.520
Once that happens, everything goes smoothly.

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:30.760
Professor says all that stuff, 
but really, he likes you.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:38.450
I already know that.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.910
And you like the professor, too, right?

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.050
Hey, don't tell anybody.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.620
My dignity is at stake, you know?

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:51.170
While you were in Osaka, 
he was always saying to me,

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:55.840
"How is Yasaburo doing? Has 
he been eaten by Benten?"

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.010
That's good to hear.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.760
What's all this?

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.320
The tanuki acting like idiots again?

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.520
The Ebisugawa Elite Guard?

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:37.820
The Ebisugawa Elite Guard?

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:39.700
Elite Guard?

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:44.350
Just some hoodlums that were lured 
in with free Electric Brandy.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:47.220
Getting the professor to take 
a bath was a big enough hassle,

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.520
I didn't expect the numbskull 
brothers to show up.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.960
This is precisely what you 
call the multiplier effect.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.990
Did you do something?

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:58.870
They're probably here on Uncle's orders 
to tell me to drop out of the race.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:01.780
This month the next Nise-emon 
will be selected.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:06.780
There's no telling whether 
it'll be Uncle or me...

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.630
I'm runnin' around all by myself!

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.400
'Cause nobody helps me out!

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:15.860
Seriously, my little brothers are such--

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:17.040
This again?

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:21.330
You up and left for Osaka, 
ignoring my situation!

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:24.130
My life was in danger so I had no choice.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:26.350
But this all got started because you--

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:28.250
Wait, look.

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:32.170
It's Kinkaku!

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:33.520
And Ginkaku!

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.290
Yeah, we know. 
You don't have to announce it.

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:39.520
If that's the case then you must 
also know what we came to say.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.610
You think I'm gonna just obediently drop out?

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:47.470
I figured you would say that.

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:51.140
But according to my cool 
and composed calculations,

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.550
there's no chance you'll win.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:57.830
You probably don't know this, but 
Yoshidayama is with the Ebisugawa family.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:02.750
Also, uhh, Takaragaike is allied with us.

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:05.250
We have a slew of support 
coming even from Yase.

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:08.900
Gosho is with me. Nanzenji 
won't be your ally either.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:11.300
If that's the case for Nanzenji, 
then it is for Ginkakuji, too.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:14.490
Kodaiji and Rokuhara will 
also inevitably go for me.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.190
That might be the case.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.710
That might be the case... 
Is that true? That many?

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:24.260
That's not what I heard. 
This is earthshattering.

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.450
Big Brother, don't be defeated. 
Take'em out!

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.500
We have an ace in the hole.

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:31.010
Oh yeah, ace in the hole, ace in the hole.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:32.280
What are you talking about?

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:37.210
Umm, hello, it's our ace in the hole-- 
 we can't tell you just like that.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.040
So I won't tell.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.430
I won't tell, but surrender now.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:44.870
The only one who can unite 
tanuki society is our dad,

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:47.750
and someday I'll follow in his footsteps.

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:51.940
The world has no further use for the 
pathetic young masters of the Shimogamo family.

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:52.870
Quite right!

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:54.630
Quite right!

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:08.490
<b>Bait-and-switch / Fragile</b>

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.900
You might want to bite our butts 
again, but it's not gonna happen.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:10.750
An artisan blacksmith residing in Nagahama 
reluctantly made us these iron underwear.

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:14.490
When you try to sink your teeth in, 
you'll end up chipping them.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:17.860
How about that idea! 
Big Brother sure is clever, huh.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:22.250
Trying to remove them by force is no use. We 
can't even take them off so easily ourselves.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:27.010
Thanks to you, both my Big Brother and I 
have caught a chill and are in distress.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.190
Quite right!

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:29.760
Quite right!

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:33.330
I've become aware of that 
crisis just now, Big Brother.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:36.810
It seems I'm on the verge of it.
 Feeling a bit "oh crap."

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.430
To tell the truth, me too.

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:43.540
So, hurry up and say you 
won't become Nise-emon.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:46.650
If you don't say it soon, 
things are gonna get messy in here.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.860
Like we care.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.110
Damn you guys!

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:01.820
Shut up!

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.110
Kinkaku, don't you know the bathhouse rules?

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:22.340
Number one, no using a towel in the bathtub.

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:24.810
Number two, no doing laundry.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:30.320
And number three, you must rinse 
before entering the water.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.770
No suddenly hopping in.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:35.030
You think a fool who doesn't 
know how to use bathwater

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:38.580
can become the leader of Kyoto's tanuki?

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:44.620
But you threw me in. I 
didn't go to do it myself.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:48.020
Well, fine then. So, what's 
your ace in the hole?

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.440
I'm not telling.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:51.090
I see.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.320
You won't tell?

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:01.690
If you don't tell, I'll throw 
you in here and put the lid on.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:04.470
Then you'll really catch a chill.

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:08.090
Ok, fine, I'll talk. I have a stomach ache!

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:13.450
It's about your old man. 
Do you know how he died?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:17.610
You're bringing that up now? 
Father was boiled in a hot pot.

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:20.530
You don't think that's strange?

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:24.760
How were they able to catch 
such a great tanuki so easily?

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:28.590
I'm clear-headed, so I 
thought this was strange.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.960
And then I did some 
investigating with Ginkaku.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.180
And we figured it out.

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:36.430
You figured out what?

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.470
If this truth were exposed,

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.940
I guarantee the Shimogamo 
family would never recover.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:43.280
You still wanna know?

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:44.560
What are you saying?

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:49.360
The day Uncle Shimogamo Soichiro 
was caught by the Friday Fellows,

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:52.700
it appears he was out late 
drinking with someone.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:56.390
So he got blind drunk and was careless.

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:58.750
The alcohol was fatal.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:00.110
So?

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:01.670
So,

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:06.460
the one he was drinking with that night 
has been silent all this time.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:11.310
I can't forgive that. Normally you would feel 
some responsibility and apologize to everyone, right?

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.270
As a tanuki like the rest of us!

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:16.190
Uncle was everyone's chief, after all.

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:19.420
Who was with him? Spit it out!

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:24.540
Your useless little brother,

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:27.320
Yajiro in the bottom of his well!

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.100
Cubold! Ubit's cubold!

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:48.650
Big Brother, what's going on?

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:51.880
Go home to the forest, Yashiro. 
Stay with Mother.

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:03.570
Why did you leave him behind?

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:05.590
It'll be too hard on him.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.640
You go so easy on Yashiro.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:10.940
No, it's for Yajiro's sake.

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:25.760
Yasaburo?

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:29.360
Oh, and a rare appearance by Yaichiro.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:32.110
Big Brother, how are you doing lately?

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:37.180
It's a small world so nothing 
all that unusual happens.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.790
At any rate, it's the bottom of a well.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:45.620
By the way, I heard the leaves 
in Arashiyama all fell in one night.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.510
For a small world, information sure travels.

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:51.400
Yesterday, Kaisei came 
'n was talking about it.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:53.370
Hey, Big Brother...

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:54.430
What's up?

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.020
Yajiro.

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:58.270
Oh, Big Brother.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:03.450
That's quite the grouchy voice. 
You have something to lecture me about?

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:06.960
I'm not confident I can live 
up to your expectations.

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:09.980
'Cause in any case, I'm a frog.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.460
Yajiro.

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:16.550
I have a clear memory of the 
last time I saw Father.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:22.330
That day I had gone out with 
him to visit the elders.

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:26.560
After that, he said he had 
an important appointment,

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.930
so he told me to go home ahead of him.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:35.250
It wasn't a rare thing. 
Father was always so busy.

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:39.030
He accompanied me as far as Higashioji

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:42.210
and saw me off as I got on the bus.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.800
I remember the way he looked even now.

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:52.460
Because that was the last time I saw him.

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:54.360
Big Brother...

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:57.330
What I want to ask you is,

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:02.550
where and when was the 
last time you saw Father?

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:11.300
Were you drinking with him that night?

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:15.190
Did you get drunk? What about him?

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:20.360
Did you leave Father drunk on his own?

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.860
Please tell me that's not how it was.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:30.700
Big Brother, that's exactly what happened.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:34.670
I'm the one who sent Father to his death.

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:38.920
How can that be?

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.020
You idiot!

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:50.960
What was I doing that day?

00:20:56.020 --> 00:21:01.380
Newborn me was strolling 
through Tadasu no Mori

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:04.900
and Dad waved a brief good-bye.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:10.220
Our dad Shimogamo Soichiro

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:15.440
was a great tanuki who united tanuki society, 
and was extremely busy.

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:18.470
He was constantly going out,

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:22.030
waving bye to the forest 
where his wife and children waited.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:25.200
That's how it was,

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:29.750
so that winter when we found out

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:32.760
he had been boiled in a year-end hot pot,

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:39.950
we had a really hard time grasping 
that that had been a true farewell.

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:49.570
As long as you live, 
there's no way to escape saying good-bye.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:59.730
That goes for humans, 
tengu, and tanuki alike.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:34.280
If not a frog I wonder what 
I would have transformed into?

00:23:34.280 --> 00:23:36.470
A newt? A salamander?

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:39.780
Either way I'd probably 
still be holed up in a well.

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:40.220
<b>The Day of Dad's Departure</b>
